// Vitest Snapshot v1, https://vitest.dev/guide/snapshot.html

exports[`the manual, pinned exactly as it reads today > pins every tab on a detour 1`] = `
{
  "AFTER": "AshwakeBACK RELICS AND THE SHOPPoints are what a run is worth. Relics buy the NEXT one — and both come out of the same pockets.Spend them in THE SHOP: on the end screen, or from the front door between runs.Relics are yours on every world; what you BUY with them stays in the world you bought it in.PERKS are not for sale. They are FOUND, out in the world, and they belong to that world. One is worn at a time.DETAILSA SACRIFICE pays 1 relic for every tile in the pocket.Reaching somewhere NEW pays 2 on its own — the half that costs you nothing.Ground that has come back — a shrine you woke, a find you took — pays its tiles or its points, but never relics twice.When a run ends, only 5% of the luck still in your purse comes home — so luck is for spending, not for saving.HOW A RUN ENDSOut of tiles with nothing ripe to POP: broke. Walking to caches is how you avoid it.A frontier that is all wall: walled in. Rare, and worth avoiding on the way past.WHAT REMAINSNothing. The ground you reveal and the territories you claim last exactly as long as this run.MENU, at the top of this panel, says which game this is and holds every way out of it.DETAILSEach territory held starts every later run with +6 tiles, up to +24.THIS BUILDOne endless plane, grown from seed 4. Same seed, same world — share the number to share the run.In play: destinations · biomes · rare tiles · the luck purse · relics + the shop · colour personalities · the stash · hidden finds · SACRIFICE LUCK.DETAILSRunning an unlabelled build.Start with 22 tiles · a placement costs 1, +1 per 22 placed · 3-card draft plus the stash.SETTINGS — the MENU tab’s own button, or MORE on the front door — holds the look, the sound and a way to replay the teaching cards.?ff=debug.overlay adds a raw readout in the hint line and the footer, for reporting a bug with no console to hand.",
  "HAND": "AshwakeBACK RARE TILESMAGIC is wild: it matches every neighbour whatever the colour, and they match it back.UNIQUE is wild and heavy: every match it makes counts DOUBLE, for both sides.A placed rare tile wears a star, so its power stays findable on a full map.✦✦A placed rare wears a star in its own colour: magic, then unique.THE STASHThe dashed HOLD card keeps one tile for later. Tap to stash the selected card; tap it again to trade that tile back.Held tiles survive a redraw — save a rare, or the colour a pocket is waiting for.▲ GREEN■ REDHOLDThe dashed slot is the stash. Tap it to keep the selected card for later.THE LUCK PURSELuck buys nothing by itself. You spend it, on the row under your hand.Every pop pays about 9 luck flat plus a little per tile, so many small pops earn far more luck than one monster.DETAILSREDRAW (12) — throw this hand away for a new one.A COLOUR’S NAME (30) — draw a new hand leaning that way, and keep the next 6 draws leaning with it. How you go and get the colour a pocket needs.FORGE (75) — turn the selected card UNIQUE. The only way to have a rare exactly when you want one.SACRIFICE LUCK — turn your whole purse into relics now, at 15%. Three times what unspent luck banks if you die on it. Needs 20 luck.",
  "PLAY": "AshwakeBACK PLACEEvery tile must touch what you have already built — that is what the glowing edges mark.The faint number is exactly what the tile pays there. A promise, not an estimate.21Glowing edges are where a tile may go. The faint number is what it would pay.DETAILSA placement costs 1 tiles, +1 for every 22 you have ever placed this run. It never comes back down — that is the clock that ends every run.You may place while ANY tiles remain — the difference is forgiven at zero, and it cannot chain: only a pop can lift you back above zero.RIPENSurrounded on all six sides, a tile RIPENS and shows its WORTH: how many neighbours match it.Stone, walls and the map’s edge all surround. Only RED counts stone as a match.POPA POCKET is a ripe tile and every ripe tile touching it. They pop together, as one.Tap any ripe tile to price its pocket. The buttons show what it pays; the biggest is priced by default.Popped tiles turn to STONE: still surrounds, never matches. Every pop makes that ground poorer.WAIT and it pays more: every tile added raises its neighbours’ worth.POP NOW for luck and steering: luck arrives mostly per pop, and each pop tilts your next draws toward its own colour.Wait too long and you die broke, with a fortune still in the ground.443Ripe tiles that touch are ONE pocket — they pop together, and leave stone.DETAILSA pop scores the pocket’s summed worth × its SIZE BONUS — one per tile in the pocket — × the distance multiplier, which rises by 1 every 3 hexes from home.The size bonus stops growing past 20 tiles: a bigger pocket pays more worth, but no more multiplier.TREASURE AND SACRIFICEInstead of popping, a pocket of 10+ can be taken as TREASURE: a MAGIC tile into your stash, or a UNIQUE one from 20+.SACRIFICE spends it a third way: no tiles, no score, relics for the shop.Every one of these destroys the pocket. Read the buttons before you tap.THE COLOURSFour grounds, four ways to score.▲ GREEN — crowds. Wants to be one big mob of its own colour.◆ YELLOW — company. Scores in messy mixed ground where nothing else matches.■ RED — ash. Builds along the spent, popped land everyone else abandons.● BLUE — tide. Worth little at home, a lot on the frontier.DETAILSGREEN: +1 worth per neighbour of its own colour past the first.YELLOW: +1 worth per differently-coloured neighbour.RED: stone and walls both count as matches for it.BLUE: +1 worth per 6 hexes from home.THE WORLDThe plane exists only where you have grown it. Every placement reveals the ground around itself.Dotted ground is a NATIVE FIELD: a tile of that colour there gains one extra match. Whole regions of one colour are BIOMES.Walls surround but never match, and cannot be built on. A frontier that is all wall ends a run.The glows beyond your ground are destinations. Touch one with a tile to claim it; each pays once.✚CACHE — 6 tiles on the spot, +4 per ring out.★SITE — points, and a BOUNTY: pop 8+ tiles within 6 hexes of the star and that pop scores ×3.❖TERRITORY — the ground around it becomes your field, for good.◈SHRINE — a system switched on for your world, permanently.DETAILSCaches and sites re-arm every run, so ground you know stays worth walking.The near world is deliberately sparse. The deeper you push, the thicker the lights and the richer the caches.Something else is hidden out there, deep and unmarked. It never glows — you stumble onto it, or you never know it was there.THE SCREENTILES keeps you alive · POINTS is your score so far · LUCK is what pops pay and the shop spends · REACH is how far you have built, and it pays at the end · COST is the next placement.Tap anything — a stat, a symbol on the map, a card — and it explains itself where it sits.Pinch or drag to move. FIT shows everything; HERE jumps back to your last tile.DETAILSTap remembered ground in the fog and every known patch of that colour lights at once — the cheapest way to see where a colour grows.Worth numbers and the map’s marks stay drawn at every zoom — small when far out, but always there.",
  "START": "AshwakeBACK THE BOARDThe board is your land. The cards below are tiles to place.Glowing edges are where you can build. The faint number is what a tile pays there.Lights out in the dark are worth walking to.✚★◈Lit is unclaimed and still pays. Faint means you have already spent it.YOUR TURNTap a card, then tap a glowing hex.Ring a tile on all six sides and it RIPENS.Tap a ripe tile, then POP. Pops pay the TILES that keep you placing.3Six sides covered: the middle tile is ripe, and worth what matches it.WHYGo DEEP. The same pocket scores far more the farther from home you pop it.This run is a visit: nothing is banked, nothing is kept, your own world is untouched.So play for the SCORE — one board, one sitting, on the plain economy everybody gets.WHICH GAMERIGHT NOW: A SHARED RUN. Nothing below about keeping or buying applies here.DETAILSYOUR WORLD — one of three this device keeps. Remembered between runs, played with everything you have bought and found.A SHARED RUN — a link with a seed in it. Somebody else’s world, played plain: no upgrades, no perk, nothing kept.THE DAILY — one world everybody gets for that date. Played plain, your tries counted, your own world untouched.SHARE, on the end screen, turns your run into such a link.",
}
`;

exports[`the manual, pinned exactly as it reads today > pins every tab under a tuning that flips every conditional sentence 1`] = `
{
  "AFTER": "AshwakeBACK HOW A RUN ENDSOut of tiles with nothing ripe to POP: broke. Walking to caches is how you avoid it.A frontier that is all wall: walled in. Rare, and worth avoiding on the way past.WHAT REMAINSGround you revealed stays drawn faint on later runs, and territories you claimed greet you already yours.THE SURVEY is five standing goals for the world itself — reach, ground known, territories held. Each pays relics once.MENU, at the top of this panel, holds your world’s own numbers, its survey, and every way out of a run.THIS BUILDOne endless plane, grown from seed 4. Same seed, same world — share the number to share the run.In play: destinations · biomes · rare tiles · the luck purse · colour personalities · hidden finds · the survey.DETAILSRunning an unlabelled build.Start with 22 tiles · a placement costs 1, +1 per 22 placed · 3-card draft.SETTINGS — the MENU tab’s own button, or MORE on the front door — holds the look, the sound and a way to replay the teaching cards.?ff=debug.overlay adds a raw readout in the hint line and the footer, for reporting a bug with no console to hand.",
  "HAND": "AshwakeBACK RARE TILESMAGIC is wild: it matches every neighbour whatever the colour, and they match it back.UNIQUE is wild and heavy: every match it makes counts DOUBLE, for both sides.A placed rare tile wears a star, so its power stays findable on a full map.✦✦A placed rare wears a star in its own colour: magic, then unique.THE LUCK PURSELuck buys nothing by itself. You spend it, on the row under your hand.Every pop pays about 0 luck flat plus a little per tile, so many small pops earn far more luck than one monster.DETAILSREDRAW (12) — throw this hand away for a new one.A COLOUR’S NAME (30) — draw a new hand leaning that way, and keep the next 0 draws leaning with it. How you go and get the colour a pocket needs.FORGE (75) — turn the selected card UNIQUE. The only way to have a rare exactly when you want one.",
  "PLAY": "AshwakeBACK PLACEEvery tile must touch what you have already built — that is what the glowing edges mark.The faint number is exactly what the tile pays there. A promise, not an estimate.21Glowing edges are where a tile may go. The faint number is what it would pay.DETAILSA placement costs 1 tiles, +1 for every 22 you have ever placed this run. It never comes back down — that is the clock that ends every run.You may place while ANY tiles remain — the difference is forgiven at zero, and it cannot chain: only a pop can lift you back above zero.RIPENSurrounded on all six sides, a tile RIPENS and shows its WORTH: how many neighbours match it.Stone, walls and the map’s edge all surround; none of them match.POPA POCKET is a ripe tile and every ripe tile touching it. They pop together, as one.Tap any ripe tile to price its pocket. The buttons show what it pays; the biggest is priced by default.Popped tiles turn to STONE: still surrounds, never matches. Every pop makes that ground poorer.WAIT and it pays more: every tile added raises its neighbours’ worth.Wait too long and you die broke, with a fortune still in the ground.443Ripe tiles that touch are ONE pocket — they pop together, and leave stone.DETAILSA pop scores the pocket’s summed worth × its SIZE BONUS — one per tile in the pocket — × the distance multiplier, which rises by 1 every 3 hexes from home.THE COLOURSFour grounds, four ways to score.▲ GREEN — crowds. Wants to be one big mob of its own colour.◆ YELLOW — company. Scores in messy mixed ground where nothing else matches.■ RED — ash. Builds along the spent, popped land everyone else abandons.● BLUE — tide. Worth little at home, a lot on the frontier.DETAILSGREEN: +1 worth per neighbour of its own colour past the first.YELLOW: +1 worth per differently-coloured neighbour.RED: stone and walls both count as matches for it.BLUE: +1 worth per 6 hexes from home.THE WORLDThe plane exists only where you have grown it. Every placement reveals the ground around itself.Dotted ground is a NATIVE FIELD: a tile of that colour there gains one extra match. Whole regions of one colour are BIOMES.Walls surround but never match, and cannot be built on. A frontier that is all wall ends a run.The glows beyond your ground are destinations. Touch one with a tile to claim it; each pays once.✚CACHE — 6 tiles on the spot.★SITE — points, and a BOUNTY: pop 8+ tiles within 6 hexes of the star and that pop scores ×3.❖TERRITORY — the ground around it becomes your field, for good.◈SHRINE — a system switched on for your world, permanently.DETAILSCaches and sites re-arm every run, so ground you know stays worth walking.The near world is deliberately sparse. The deeper you push, the thicker the lights and the richer the caches.Something else is hidden out there, deep and unmarked. It never glows — you stumble onto it, or you never know it was there.THE SCREENTILES keeps you alive · POINTS is your score so far · LUCK is what pops pay and the shop spends · REACH is how far you have built, and it pays at the end · COST is the next placement.Tap anything — a stat, a symbol on the map, a card — and it explains itself where it sits.Pinch or drag to move. FIT shows everything; HERE jumps back to your last tile.DETAILSTap remembered ground in the fog and every known patch of that colour lights at once — the cheapest way to see where a colour grows.Worth numbers and the map’s marks stay drawn at every zoom — small when far out, but always there.",
  "START": "AshwakeBACK THE BOARDThe board is your land. The cards below are tiles to place.Glowing edges are where you can build. The faint number is what a tile pays there.Lights out in the dark are worth walking to.✚★◈Lit is unclaimed and still pays. Faint means you have already spent it.YOUR TURNTap a card, then tap a glowing hex.Ring a tile on all six sides and it RIPENS.Tap a ripe tile, then POP. Pops pay the TILES that keep you placing.3Six sides covered: the middle tile is ripe, and worth what matches it.WHYGo DEEP. The same pocket scores far more the farther from home you pop it.Runs end. What you carry out buys upgrades, so the next run starts stronger.Your world remembers: ground stays revealed, territories stay yours.WHICH GAMERIGHT NOW: YOUR OWN WORLD — everything in this manual applies.DETAILSYOUR WORLD — one of three this device keeps. Remembered between runs, played with everything you have bought and found.A SHARED RUN — a link with a seed in it. Somebody else’s world, played plain: no upgrades, no perk, nothing kept.THE DAILY — one world everybody gets for that date. Played plain, your tries counted, your own world untouched.SHARE, on the end screen, turns your run into such a link.",
}
`;

